0. Overview
-----------

    Braving is an independently branded browser based on exact Brave
    and Chromium releases, featuring a maintainable mutator-based architecture.

    Braving does not simply rebrand an APK. It builds directly from clean
    upstream source code with reproducible, mutator-driven modifications.


1. Architecture Overview
------------------------

    User selects BRAVE_VERSION
              |
    matching brave-core release
              |
    exact Chromium revision
              |
    Braving mutators
              |
    Braving source
              |
    reproducible Braving build
              |
    Braving APK / AAB


2. Repository Structure
-----------------------

    Braving/
    |-- branding/            Master vector identity, Android drawables, static PNGs
    |   |-- android/         Vector logo drawables, adaptive and themed icons
    |   `-- brave-core-static/ 156 static PNGs and 10 SVGs for brave-core overlay
    |-- docs/                Architecture, building, debloating, and release docs
    |-- metadata/            Release manifests and exact upstream commits
    |   `-- releases/        Generated release manifests (package_id, commits, arch)
    |-- patches/             Unified patches for branding, debloating, and updater
    |   `-- android/
    |       |-- 0001-braving-branding.patch
    |       |-- 0002-custom-updater-endpoint.patch
    |       `-- debloat/     Modular enterprise debloating patches
    `-- scripts/             Modular build, mutator, signing, and verification suite
        |-- android/         Android build orchestration and Python mutators
        |   |-- apply-assets.sh      Applies static raster and vector branding assets
        |   |-- apply-branding.py    GRD/GRDP string de-branding and XTB remapping
        |   |-- apply-features.py    GN build fixes and WebUI bundle decoupling
        |   |-- build-android.sh     Phase 2: Compiles the release Braving APK
        |   |-- filter-build-log.py  Real-time CI stream filter preventing log truncation
        |   |-- prepare-source.sh    Phase 1: Dynamic checkout, patches, & mutators
        |   |-- sign-apk.sh          v1/v2/v3 APK release signing & verification
        |   |-- verify-all.sh        Master 5-step verification suite
        |   `-- verify-branding.sh   Validates AAPT2 limits & complete de-branding
        |-- download-cache.sh Distributed CI Siso warm cache restore
        |-- upload-cache.sh   Distributed CI Siso warm cache chunker and upload
        `-- tests/            Automated unit and integration test suite


3. Building Braving
-------------------

3.1. Prerequisites

    Building Braving requires a Linux environment (x86_64 or aarch64).
    You will need the following tools installed:

      - Node.js >= 24.16.0
      - pnpm >= 11.11.0
      - Python 3.10+
      - JDK 17+
      - Android SDK & NDK (for mobile builds)


3.2. Prepare Source

    To validate revisions, checkout the source code, and apply Braving
    branding mutators, run the preparation script with the desired
    Brave version (or omit to auto-resolve latest stable):

        ./scripts/android/prepare-source.sh [BRAVE_VERSION]


3.3. Build Braving APK

    Once the source is prepared, compile the release APK:

        ./scripts/android/build-android.sh --arch=arm64 --release


